1
00:00:08,952 --> 00:00:10,993
<i>Previously on</i> From...

2
00:00:11,035 --> 00:00:13,835
You ever wonder
if Abby was right?

3
00:00:13,877 --> 00:00:15,517
What if it's all just a dream?

4
00:00:15,559 --> 00:00:16,878
Who did you come here with?

5
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:20,842
My mother.
She was nice.

6
00:00:20,884 --> 00:00:22,164
What are you drawing?

7
00:00:22,206 --> 00:00:23,445
Things I've seen.

8
00:00:23,487 --> 00:00:25,687
It's good to draw them
when you see them

9
00:00:25,729 --> 00:00:28,890
<i>so even if you forget,</i>
<i>pictures remember.</i>

10
00:00:28,932 --> 00:00:32,734
When Christopher
started seeing
that symbol, things changed.

11
00:00:32,776 --> 00:00:35,297
<i>He changed. Everyone died.</i>

12
00:00:35,339 --> 00:00:36,738
I've seen this.

13
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:38,260
Yeah, like in
a vision or something?

14
00:00:38,302 --> 00:00:39,861
No, on the walls
in the tunnels.

15
00:00:39,903 --> 00:00:41,503
What tunnels?

16
00:00:41,545 --> 00:00:43,105
You heard
the voice on the radio.

17
00:00:43,147 --> 00:00:47,949
That means that there are
people out there
who can see us.

18
00:00:47,991 --> 00:00:51,353
And what part of you thinks
that that's a good sign?

19
00:00:51,395 --> 00:00:54,396
You already got people's hopes
up with your goddamn tower...

20
00:00:54,438 --> 00:00:55,517
All the more reason that we...

21
00:00:55,559 --> 00:00:57,881
To keep our fucking
mouths shut.

22
00:00:59,363 --> 00:01:01,883
What if I told you
that drone might get you home

23
00:01:01,925 --> 00:01:04,206
in time for
your nephew's birthday?

24
00:01:04,248 --> 00:01:07,329
Experiments have been
going on like this
for a long, long time.

25
00:01:07,371 --> 00:01:08,530
This radio's pretty trashed.

26
00:01:08,572 --> 00:01:09,851
Well, the radio's
not the problem.

27
00:01:09,893 --> 00:01:11,653
I can handle the radio.

28
00:01:11,695 --> 00:01:13,255
And it never occurred to you
that some of the people here

29
00:01:13,297 --> 00:01:14,496
might be in on it?

30
00:01:14,538 --> 00:01:16,658
How else do you keep
the experiment on track?

31
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,100
You really did it.

32
00:01:18,142 --> 00:01:19,301
You killed one of them.

33
00:01:19,343 --> 00:01:20,662
What do we do
with the body?

34
00:01:20,704 --> 00:01:22,424
This is our chance
to learn about them.

35
00:01:22,466 --> 00:01:24,746
We can open them up, see what
they look like on the inside.

36
00:01:24,788 --> 00:01:25,827
Fuck!
Stop!

37
00:01:25,869 --> 00:01:26,908
Fuckin' piece of shit!
Okay, stop it!

38
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:29,071
Stop! Hey!
Kristi, hey, hey! Stop!

39
00:01:29,113 --> 00:01:30,392
You really think
injecting them

40
00:01:30,434 --> 00:01:31,793
with that stuff's gonna
kill them?

41
00:01:31,835 --> 00:01:33,755
Honestly, I got
no fucking idea.

42
00:01:33,797 --> 00:01:35,637
It's the
best chance we got.

43
00:01:35,679 --> 00:01:37,559
How are we even
gonna test it?

44
00:01:37,601 --> 00:01:38,760
I do have this
little trick though.

45
00:01:38,802 --> 00:01:41,002
For when things really
start to get to me.

46
00:01:41,044 --> 00:01:43,925
I fill up the bathtub
and I sink down just enough

47
00:01:43,967 --> 00:01:45,927
<i>so that the water</i>
<i>is level with my ears,</i>

48
00:01:45,969 --> 00:01:48,332
<i>and I just sit like that</i>
<i>for a while, and I breathe.</i>

49
00:02:02,426 --> 00:02:04,065
Ma.

50
00:02:39,983 --> 00:02:41,383
Hello?

51
00:02:41,425 --> 00:02:43,985
<i>They touch,</i>
<i>they break, they steal.</i>

52
00:02:44,027 --> 00:02:46,268
<i>No one here is free.</i>

53
00:02:46,310 --> 00:02:47,909
Hello?

54
00:02:47,951 --> 00:02:52,073
<i>Here they come,</i>
<i>they come for three,</i>

55
00:02:52,115 --> 00:02:53,395
<i>unless you stop the melody.</i>

56
00:02:53,437 --> 00:02:55,439
Who is this?

57
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:59,603
<i>They touch,</i>
<i>they break, they steal...</i>

58
00:03:49,493 --> 00:03:51,495
What the fuck?

59
00:06:01,144 --> 00:06:03,146
So what's the point?

60
00:06:05,268 --> 00:06:07,589
Well, I told you,
once we re-establish
connection

61
00:06:07,631 --> 00:06:09,070
we can start as--
No, no, no, no, no.

62
00:06:09,112 --> 00:06:11,114
Not the antenna.
I'm talking about this.

63
00:06:12,436 --> 00:06:15,236
Let's say this is
one real big experiment.

64
00:06:15,278 --> 00:06:16,638
For what?

65
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:20,722
Well, there's a lot
of value in seeing

66
00:06:20,764 --> 00:06:23,246
how far you can push
someone before they break.

67
00:06:24,928 --> 00:06:26,930
Look what this place
did to that girl Sara.

68
00:06:28,291 --> 00:06:29,891
The one that
tried to hurt your kid?

69
00:06:29,933 --> 00:06:31,935
Yeah.

70
00:06:32,375 --> 00:06:35,739
I'll tell you, the fact
that she's still breathing,

71
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:39,781
you got a lot more
restraint than I do.

72
00:06:39,823 --> 00:06:43,144
I'm not gonna let this place
turn me into
something I'm not.

73
00:06:43,186 --> 00:06:45,627
Shit, they really
wanna break people,

74
00:06:45,669 --> 00:06:48,149
I got a few ex-girlfriends
they could hire.

75
00:06:51,915 --> 00:06:52,994
All right,
let's give it a shot.

76
00:06:53,036 --> 00:06:54,075
All right.

77
00:07:01,284 --> 00:07:02,884
There we are.

78
00:07:02,926 --> 00:07:04,045
Keep going.

79
00:07:04,087 --> 00:07:06,089
Yup.

80
00:07:08,371 --> 00:07:09,891
Well, go, go higher.

81
00:07:09,933 --> 00:07:11,935
Uh, that's it.

82
00:07:12,375 --> 00:07:13,415
What?

83
00:07:13,457 --> 00:07:15,459
That's it!

84
00:07:17,501 --> 00:07:19,503
All right,
bring it down.

85
00:07:20,744 --> 00:07:22,746
I got it. I got it.

86
00:07:26,670 --> 00:07:29,110
Look, let's say
this thing works,

87
00:07:29,152 --> 00:07:31,152
why would the people running
this thing wanna talk to you?

88
00:07:31,194 --> 00:07:33,114
They already
did it once.

89
00:07:33,156 --> 00:07:35,437
Were they trying to help
or were they just tryin'
to fuck with your head?

90
00:07:35,479 --> 00:07:37,118
I mean, look at this,
look at where we are.

91
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:39,400
Listen, if you don't
wanna help, you...

92
00:07:39,442 --> 00:07:41,723
I'm not saying that,
I just...

93
00:07:41,765 --> 00:07:43,204
Look, if someone out here
really wanted to help,

94
00:07:43,246 --> 00:07:45,406
they would find
a way to help.

95
00:07:45,448 --> 00:07:48,131
I still think we'd be
better off looking at
the people in here.

96
00:07:48,932 --> 00:07:50,612
Like, something this big.

97
00:07:50,654 --> 00:07:52,333
You'd have to have
someone on the inside.

98
00:07:52,375 --> 00:07:54,335
Ah, you can't just start
throwing around accusations...

99
00:07:54,377 --> 00:07:56,500
I'm not saying accuse,
I just...

100
00:07:57,821 --> 00:08:00,542
When you got here,
who told you what was what?

101
00:08:00,584 --> 00:08:02,586
Who laid out
all the rules?

102
00:08:03,667 --> 00:08:07,108
Boyd, Donna, Father Khatri.

103
00:08:07,150 --> 00:08:08,309
Father who?

104
00:08:08,351 --> 00:08:10,431
Khatri.
He died.

105
00:08:10,473 --> 00:08:12,634
That night they got
into the Colony House.

106
00:08:12,676 --> 00:08:13,715
Well, did you see it?

107
00:08:13,757 --> 00:08:14,956
See what?

108
00:08:14,998 --> 00:08:17,000
Did you see
the priest get killed?

109
00:08:17,561 --> 00:08:18,760
No.

110
00:08:18,802 --> 00:08:20,361
It happened outside
the Sheriff's station.

111
00:08:20,403 --> 00:08:22,405
I wasn't there.

112
00:08:23,887 --> 00:08:25,887
Right.

113
00:08:25,929 --> 00:08:28,890
And of all the people that
died since you've been here,

114
00:08:28,932 --> 00:08:31,374
how many times have you
actually seen it happen?

115
00:08:32,215 --> 00:08:34,215
What's your point?

116
00:08:34,257 --> 00:08:37,458
Well, what if the people
these "monsters" are killing,

117
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:39,701
what if they're
all in on it?

118
00:08:39,743 --> 00:08:41,222
I mean, you wanna scare
the shit outta people,

119
00:08:41,264 --> 00:08:42,784
you need
a body count, right?

120
00:08:42,826 --> 00:08:45,266
Maybe that's why they
say when you get here,

121
00:08:45,308 --> 00:08:47,228
you gotta keep
your blinds down.

122
00:08:47,270 --> 00:08:49,831
'Cause God forbid
you're lookin'
out your window at night.

123
00:08:49,873 --> 00:08:51,875
No.

124
00:08:52,796 --> 00:08:54,798
What about
that guy, Brick?

125
00:08:55,118 --> 00:08:56,117
What about Tom?

126
00:08:56,159 --> 00:08:59,080
I didn't see it happen.
Did you?

127
00:08:59,122 --> 00:09:01,042
I mean, yeah,
I saw a body the next day,

128
00:09:01,084 --> 00:09:04,566
but I didn't get close enough
to see if that shit was real.

129
00:09:04,608 --> 00:09:06,648
Have you seen one ounce
of proof that anyone here
has actually...

130
00:09:06,690 --> 00:09:07,809
Nathan.

131
00:09:07,851 --> 00:09:09,130
What?

132
00:09:09,172 --> 00:09:11,174
Sara's brother.

133
00:09:12,015 --> 00:09:14,658
She killed him,
slit his throat.

134
00:09:16,419 --> 00:09:18,421
Or she didn't.

135
00:09:20,463 --> 00:09:22,143
Let's just imagine for
a second that I'm right,

136
00:09:22,185 --> 00:09:24,505
and everyone here
that dies is in on it.

137
00:09:24,547 --> 00:09:25,707
It's gonna mean
one of two things.

138
00:09:25,749 --> 00:09:28,710
One, they pushed Sara
so far that

139
00:09:28,752 --> 00:09:31,392
she actually killed someone,
which, you know,
maybe she did.

140
00:09:31,434 --> 00:09:34,235
Or, like everything else,
that whole thing with Nathan,

141
00:09:34,277 --> 00:09:36,960
him arriving just in
time to save your kid,

142
00:09:38,081 --> 00:09:40,083
what if that's
all just for show?

143
00:09:43,967 --> 00:09:46,329
Maybe poor little Sara's
not as broken as you think.

144
00:09:57,861 --> 00:09:59,300
Hey, Sara.

145
00:09:59,342 --> 00:10:01,903
I was gonna
come by and check on you...

146
00:10:01,945 --> 00:10:03,424
I wanna go back out.

147
00:10:03,466 --> 00:10:04,545
Excuse me?

148
00:10:04,587 --> 00:10:06,227
To the woods.
I wanna go back.

149
00:10:06,269 --> 00:10:08,750
I'll pack a bag,
take a talisman.

150
00:10:08,792 --> 00:10:10,872
What if you were right?

151
00:10:10,914 --> 00:10:12,193
What if the answers
are out there?

152
00:10:12,235 --> 00:10:14,435
Maybe we just didn't
go out far enough.

153
00:10:14,477 --> 00:10:16,638
Well, we went far enough
that whatever's out there

154
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:18,682
put us right
the fuck back here.

155
00:10:19,482 --> 00:10:20,682
So that's it?

156
00:10:20,724 --> 00:10:22,363
We just give up?

157
00:10:22,405 --> 00:10:23,524
I didn't say that.

158
00:10:23,566 --> 00:10:25,286
I get it.
People need you here.

159
00:10:25,328 --> 00:10:27,849
You shouldn't be out there,
but I can...

160
00:10:27,891 --> 00:10:29,170
Just let me do this.

161
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:31,292
Okay. Why...

162
00:10:31,334 --> 00:10:32,573
Why do you wanna
go out there?

163
00:10:32,615 --> 00:10:33,855
Because I wanna help.

164
00:10:33,897 --> 00:10:35,777
I'm sure you do,

165
00:10:35,819 --> 00:10:38,301
but that's not why
you wanna leave. So...

166
00:10:39,783 --> 00:10:41,502
There's no place for me here.

167
00:10:41,544 --> 00:10:45,466
No one even wants me here, and
they're right, I shouldn't...

168
00:10:45,508 --> 00:10:48,029
This is something
I can do.

169
00:10:48,071 --> 00:10:51,833
There's a difference
between going out there

170
00:10:51,875 --> 00:10:53,194
and running away from here.

171
00:10:53,236 --> 00:10:55,877
Leaving? That'd feel good.
It'd be easy.

172
00:10:55,919 --> 00:10:57,921
We don't get to do
easy anymore.

173
00:11:00,964 --> 00:11:05,847
I can't just sit
in that church anymore.

174
00:11:05,889 --> 00:11:08,930
There's nothing for me to do.
Nowhere for me to go.

175
00:11:08,972 --> 00:11:13,496
Okay. Good, now we're talking
about problems we can fix.

176
00:11:18,341 --> 00:11:19,901
Down there.

177
00:11:19,943 --> 00:11:21,422
That's where
I saw your symbol,

178
00:11:21,464 --> 00:11:23,466
and it's...

179
00:11:23,987 --> 00:11:26,547
also the first time
I saw the children.

180
00:11:26,589 --> 00:11:28,750
And those, uh, those things
that come out at night,

181
00:11:28,792 --> 00:11:30,191
they're down there too?

182
00:11:30,233 --> 00:11:31,993
Yeah.

183
00:11:32,035 --> 00:11:33,114
All right.

184
00:11:33,156 --> 00:11:35,516
This has to mean something.
It can't...

185
00:11:35,558 --> 00:11:36,637
It can't be a coincidence.

186
00:11:36,679 --> 00:11:38,039
Why?

187
00:11:38,081 --> 00:11:40,323
How much do you know
about chaos theory?

188
00:11:43,566 --> 00:11:47,010
A butterfly... a butterfly
flaps its wings in Wyoming.

189
00:11:48,611 --> 00:11:53,054
A month later there's
a tsunami in Japan,

190
00:11:53,096 --> 00:11:56,417
and on the surface
the two events
appear entirely unrelated

191
00:11:56,459 --> 00:12:00,541
but in reality there is
an intricate set
of connections...

192
00:12:00,583 --> 00:12:02,423
Jade, what the fuck
are you talking about?

193
00:12:02,465 --> 00:12:03,865
It's not an accident.
We just...

194
00:12:03,907 --> 00:12:06,309
We need more information
to see how they're connected.

195
00:12:07,430 --> 00:12:09,070
Well, I'm not gonna
go back in there.

196
00:12:09,112 --> 00:12:11,552
Yeah, no shit.

197
00:12:11,594 --> 00:12:13,596
I mean,
you'd have to be crazy...

198
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:16,517
Motherfucker.

199
00:12:16,559 --> 00:12:17,919
What?

200
00:12:17,961 --> 00:12:19,721
Did Victor see it?

201
00:12:19,763 --> 00:12:21,682
You told me Victor
was down there with you.

202
00:12:21,724 --> 00:12:23,124
Did he see the symbol
on the walls?

203
00:12:23,166 --> 00:12:24,926
Of course. He was
the one that pointed it out.

204
00:12:24,968 --> 00:12:28,329
Of course. I asked him.
I asked him, point blank.

205
00:12:28,371 --> 00:12:30,051
He promised to tell me
everything he knew

206
00:12:30,093 --> 00:12:34,097
about that symbol, yet somehow
he manages to leave out...

207
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:39,700
You know, in the entire
Venn diagram of crazy that

208
00:12:39,742 --> 00:12:42,425
you and I have seen
there's one
single point of overlap.

209
00:12:58,601 --> 00:13:00,321
Hi.

210
00:13:00,363 --> 00:13:02,365
Uh, is Ethan home?

211
00:13:03,166 --> 00:13:05,368
Um, yeah.
Yeah, yeah. Come on in.

212
00:13:07,130 --> 00:13:09,170
I'll...
I'll wait out here.

213
00:13:09,212 --> 00:13:11,214
Okay.

214
00:13:12,335 --> 00:13:14,697
Ethan!
Victor's here!

215
00:13:20,864 --> 00:13:23,584
You know,
I never got to thank you

216
00:13:23,626 --> 00:13:26,988
for everything that you did
that night at Colony House.

217
00:13:27,030 --> 00:13:29,590
I mean,
getting me out of there.
You saved my life.

218
00:13:29,632 --> 00:13:31,192
Okay.

219
00:13:31,234 --> 00:13:33,034
Hi.

220
00:13:33,076 --> 00:13:34,275
Hi.

221
00:13:34,317 --> 00:13:35,837
'Kay. I'll be ready
in two minutes.

222
00:13:35,879 --> 00:13:37,118
Okay.

223
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,920
We're going to help
Mrs. Liu at the diner.

224
00:13:38,962 --> 00:13:41,122
I brought you something.

225
00:13:41,164 --> 00:13:43,524
Are you gonna come in?

226
00:13:43,566 --> 00:13:46,089
No, you have
to come outside.

227
00:13:46,489 --> 00:13:47,849
Why?

228
00:13:47,891 --> 00:13:49,893
Because you have to
try it on.

229
00:13:51,334 --> 00:13:53,254
Come.

230
00:13:53,296 --> 00:13:56,539
It's getting cold
and you'll need a coat soon.

231
00:13:58,261 --> 00:14:00,263
This used to be mine.

232
00:14:01,544 --> 00:14:03,546
Can you see if it fits?

233
00:14:04,427 --> 00:14:06,429
Yeah.

234
00:14:11,514 --> 00:14:13,636
Here.
I drew this for you.

235
00:14:16,599 --> 00:14:19,520
Uh, I don't want this.

236
00:14:19,562 --> 00:14:20,761
Why?

237
00:14:20,803 --> 00:14:22,884
Because pictures are
for things that are gone.

238
00:14:22,926 --> 00:14:25,006
But what if
something happens to me?

239
00:14:25,048 --> 00:14:26,807
You forget
a lot of stuff.

240
00:14:26,849 --> 00:14:28,209
I wouldn't want
you to forget me.

241
00:14:28,251 --> 00:14:30,693
I said,
don't talk like that.

242
00:14:32,735 --> 00:14:35,939
Well, if you don't keep it,
I don't want the coat.

243
00:14:38,221 --> 00:14:40,663
'Kay, you ready?
We gotta go.

244
00:14:42,906 --> 00:14:44,908
Wanna come?

245
00:14:46,589 --> 00:14:48,029
Okay.

246
00:14:48,071 --> 00:14:50,073
Come on.

247
00:14:51,154 --> 00:14:52,713
Nice jacket.

248
00:14:52,755 --> 00:14:54,757
Thanks.

249
00:14:55,278 --> 00:14:57,518
Are you sure
you shouldn't be in bed?

250
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:59,080
I mean, no, I'm fine.

251
00:14:59,122 --> 00:15:01,562
You know, I'm not gonna be
doing any push-ups
anytime soon,

252
00:15:01,604 --> 00:15:05,006
but I feel great.
Seriously.

253
00:15:05,048 --> 00:15:07,088
Did Kristi
check you out?

254
00:15:07,130 --> 00:15:10,011
Yeah, yeah, and she's more
surprised than you.

255
00:15:10,053 --> 00:15:12,253
And what about Dale?

256
00:15:12,295 --> 00:15:13,774
Donna's locked him
up in his room.

257
00:15:13,816 --> 00:15:15,818
Dad, everything's fine.

258
00:15:19,342 --> 00:15:20,541
What are you smiling about?

259
00:15:23,546 --> 00:15:24,946
I have some news.

260
00:15:24,988 --> 00:15:27,468
Corey said you were
looking for me?

261
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:30,954
Oh, yeah, I'll uh...
Uh, one sec. Yeah.

262
00:15:33,316 --> 00:15:35,318
I'll tell you later.

263
00:15:38,241 --> 00:15:39,400
Okay. Get some rest.

264
00:15:39,442 --> 00:15:40,441
All right, Dad.

265
00:15:40,483 --> 00:15:42,485
Look, Dad I'm good,
but go ahead.

266
00:15:45,248 --> 00:15:47,250
Hey.

267
00:15:48,651 --> 00:15:50,651
Are you out of
your fucking mind?

268
00:15:50,693 --> 00:15:52,333
I really don't
need this today, Boyd.

269
00:15:52,375 --> 00:15:54,255
I have a headache like
you would not believe.

270
00:15:54,297 --> 00:15:55,937
I'm not asking you
to let her stay here.

271
00:15:55,979 --> 00:15:57,338
Look, just throw me a bone.

272
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:59,660
Give her something to do.
Anything. I don't care.

273
00:15:59,702 --> 00:16:01,943
She just wants
to feel useful.

274
00:16:01,985 --> 00:16:04,065
Okay. I'll do what I can.
Thank you.

275
00:16:04,107 --> 00:16:07,548
But we have bigger problems
right now than
Sara being bored.

276
00:16:07,590 --> 00:16:10,511
I got a house full of
people on their last nerve,

277
00:16:10,553 --> 00:16:12,193
a madman locked
in the bedroom,

278
00:16:12,235 --> 00:16:15,476
and last night Elgin
almost drowned in his sleep.

279
00:16:15,518 --> 00:16:18,119
What? He what?

280
00:16:20,083 --> 00:16:22,085
Come in.

281
00:16:22,445 --> 00:16:24,085
Hey.

282
00:16:24,127 --> 00:16:26,127
I heard about what
happened last night.

283
00:16:26,169 --> 00:16:27,688
What are you doing?

284
00:16:27,730 --> 00:16:30,451
I found these in
one of the closets.

285
00:16:30,493 --> 00:16:31,612
Helps me relax.

286
00:16:31,654 --> 00:16:33,656
Huh.

287
00:16:35,098 --> 00:16:37,498
Wanna tell me
about it?

288
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:39,460
This nightmare of yours.

289
00:16:39,502 --> 00:16:41,504
I was, uh...

290
00:16:42,785 --> 00:16:44,465
I was sitting
in the bathtub,

291
00:16:44,507 --> 00:16:47,348
in my dream,

292
00:16:47,390 --> 00:16:50,273
and something
pushed me under the water.

293
00:16:52,075 --> 00:16:55,436
Then I guess
someone shook me awake,

294
00:16:55,478 --> 00:16:57,999
and I started
spitting up water and uh...

295
00:16:58,041 --> 00:17:00,043
How's that even possible?

296
00:17:04,167 --> 00:17:06,527
You didn't tell anybody
about anything that happened

297
00:17:06,569 --> 00:17:07,888
at the clinic, did you?

298
00:17:11,774 --> 00:17:13,534
Well, I got
some good news.

299
00:17:13,576 --> 00:17:18,499
We, uh, pulled something
out of that thing,

300
00:17:18,541 --> 00:17:21,384
something
that might help us.

301
00:17:22,865 --> 00:17:24,425
So you think
it's like a poison?

302
00:17:24,467 --> 00:17:25,906
Well, it could be.

303
00:17:25,948 --> 00:17:28,189
The only problem is we gotta
figure out how to get this

304
00:17:28,231 --> 00:17:29,630
inside another
one of those things

305
00:17:29,672 --> 00:17:31,674
without getting
ourselves killed.

306
00:17:32,795 --> 00:17:34,917
You have a gun, right?

307
00:17:35,598 --> 00:17:37,678
Yeah.

308
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:39,722
So make some
silver bullets.

309
00:17:43,246 --> 00:17:44,285
Huh.

310
00:17:44,327 --> 00:17:45,966
No, you're making that up.

311
00:17:46,008 --> 00:17:48,529
I'm not.
Julie, tell him it's real.

312
00:17:48,571 --> 00:17:49,930
What's real?

313
00:17:49,972 --> 00:17:52,053
The Internet.

314
00:17:52,095 --> 00:17:54,055
Oh. Yeah, yeah,
that's a thing.

315
00:17:54,097 --> 00:17:55,536
Told you.

316
00:17:55,578 --> 00:17:58,099
You come carry.

317
00:17:58,141 --> 00:18:00,143
You're up.

318
00:18:01,784 --> 00:18:04,745
Are you just gonna
wear that thing all day?

319
00:18:04,787 --> 00:18:05,826
I like it.

320
00:18:05,868 --> 00:18:07,870
It smells musty.

321
00:18:11,554 --> 00:18:13,556
You put here.

322
00:18:20,723 --> 00:18:22,725
What's this?

323
00:18:24,447 --> 00:18:26,407
Where did you...

324
00:18:26,449 --> 00:18:27,928
Where did you
get that?

325
00:18:27,970 --> 00:18:29,972
It was in the pocket.

326
00:18:33,055 --> 00:18:35,057
What's wrong?

327
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:40,781
I need you to be brave.

328
00:18:40,823 --> 00:18:43,504
There you are! He's in here!

329
00:18:43,546 --> 00:18:45,666
Listen, we gotta talk.
I have to go.

330
00:18:45,708 --> 00:18:47,268
- Huh? Nah. Come here.
- Hey, what're you doing?

331
00:18:47,310 --> 00:18:48,629
Hey!
We made a deal, remember?

332
00:18:48,671 --> 00:18:50,671
I play you the song,
you tell me about the symbol.

333
00:18:50,713 --> 00:18:51,712
Hey!
Leave him alone.

334
00:18:51,754 --> 00:18:53,834
I told you
about the symbol.

335
00:18:53,876 --> 00:18:55,516
Yeah, you sure
you told me everything?

336
00:18:55,558 --> 00:18:58,279
You didn't tell me you
saw it on the wall
down in those tunnels?

337
00:18:58,321 --> 00:18:59,920
- Hey! Relax! Relax!
- What tunnel?

338
00:18:59,962 --> 00:19:01,482
Victor, we just want
to talk to you.

339
00:19:01,524 --> 00:19:02,683
No, I have to go.
Hey! Give me one reason...

340
00:19:02,725 --> 00:19:04,285
Mom, what's going on?
Stay here, honey.

341
00:19:04,327 --> 00:19:06,527
Right? One reason
why you wouldn't mention...

342
00:19:06,569 --> 00:19:08,088
Jade!
that you saw this symbol on

343
00:19:08,130 --> 00:19:10,131
the wall down
in those tunnels!

344
00:19:10,173 --> 00:19:11,932
Just give me one!
It's not important.

345
00:19:11,974 --> 00:19:14,094
Yes it is! Goddammit, stop!
Hey, Jade! Stop it!

346
00:19:14,136 --> 00:19:15,376
Stop it! Stop it!
No, no!

347
00:19:15,418 --> 00:19:17,658
I am done fucking around!
You, hey, look at me!

348
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:20,261
You don't get to pick
and choose what you tell us!

349
00:19:20,303 --> 00:19:22,263
Everything...
Everything you know,

350
00:19:22,305 --> 00:19:25,906
everything you've seen,
it all matters,

351
00:19:25,948 --> 00:19:28,391
because that may
be how we go home.

352
00:19:30,473 --> 00:19:33,794
Don't you want that?
Huh?

353
00:19:33,836 --> 00:19:35,838
Wouldn't you like
to go home?

354
00:19:40,643 --> 00:19:42,645
This is my home.

355
00:19:49,051 --> 00:19:50,371
What is wrong
with you?

356
00:19:50,413 --> 00:19:53,093
Is it just physically
impossible for you

357
00:19:53,135 --> 00:19:55,816
not to be an asshole
for longer than 10 minutes?

358
00:19:55,858 --> 00:19:57,338
Great,
you're yelling at me again.

359
00:19:57,380 --> 00:19:59,099
Fuck off.
That didn't take very long.

360
00:19:59,141 --> 00:20:01,143
Victor!

361
00:20:16,439 --> 00:20:17,918
Sara.

362
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:21,202
Uh, we were wondering
if we could
talk to you for a minute.

363
00:20:21,244 --> 00:20:22,643
About what?

364
00:20:22,685 --> 00:20:24,845
We're just trying to get
our head around a few things.

365
00:20:24,887 --> 00:20:26,207
This is Randall.
He came on...

366
00:20:26,249 --> 00:20:28,251
I know who he is.

367
00:20:28,571 --> 00:20:30,573
What do you wanna know?

368
00:20:33,256 --> 00:20:35,936
You came
with your brother.

369
00:20:35,978 --> 00:20:38,178
Where were you going?

370
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:39,540
Back to Boston.

371
00:20:39,582 --> 00:20:41,342
Where were you
coming from?

372
00:20:41,384 --> 00:20:43,386
Why does it matter?

373
00:20:45,268 --> 00:20:46,307
What's going on?

374
00:20:46,349 --> 00:20:47,668
We're just trying
to figure out

375
00:20:47,710 --> 00:20:51,071
if there's any pattern to
how people end up here.

376
00:20:51,113 --> 00:20:53,115
We just want your help.

377
00:20:55,718 --> 00:20:57,918
Pennsylvania.

378
00:20:57,960 --> 00:21:00,803
I was living in New Hope,
but it... it wasn't...

379
00:21:02,485 --> 00:21:04,485
Nathan came to
bring me back home.

380
00:21:04,527 --> 00:21:06,529
So you guys were close?

381
00:21:08,331 --> 00:21:10,333
He was my best friend.

382
00:21:11,574 --> 00:21:13,254
That day at the barn...

383
00:21:13,296 --> 00:21:15,378
No. I don't want
to talk about that.

384
00:21:19,302 --> 00:21:21,304
Sara...

385
00:21:22,985 --> 00:21:24,987
I know you didn't
want to hurt Ethan.

386
00:21:25,308 --> 00:21:27,310
I know that.

387
00:21:28,551 --> 00:21:32,112
And what this place
did to you,
it isn't fair, but please...

388
00:21:32,154 --> 00:21:34,156
Is your brother
still alive?

389
00:21:35,237 --> 00:21:36,757
What?

390
00:21:36,799 --> 00:21:38,319
It's a simple
fucking question.

391
00:21:38,361 --> 00:21:39,880
Ease up.

392
00:21:39,922 --> 00:21:41,442
The hell is going on?

393
00:21:43,686 --> 00:21:45,686
It's convenient.

394
00:21:45,728 --> 00:21:47,087
Excuse me?

395
00:21:47,129 --> 00:21:49,089
You just show up here
out of nowhere the moment

396
00:21:49,131 --> 00:21:50,691
we start asking
fucking questions?

397
00:21:50,733 --> 00:21:52,172
What the fuck are
you talking about?

398
00:21:52,214 --> 00:21:54,216
Nothing.

399
00:21:56,218 --> 00:21:58,539
Boyd says you're looking
for ways to be helpful.

400
00:21:58,581 --> 00:22:00,981
I got a bunch of clothes
that need stitching. You sew?

401
00:22:01,023 --> 00:22:02,743
Yeah.

402
00:22:02,785 --> 00:22:05,546
Great. Here you go.
You start with that.

403
00:22:05,588 --> 00:22:07,107
You two get
the fuck out.

404
00:22:07,149 --> 00:22:09,512
Who are you, huh?

405
00:22:10,713 --> 00:22:12,313
You think you're
some kinda big shot?

406
00:22:12,355 --> 00:22:14,715
Got a little power?

407
00:22:14,757 --> 00:22:17,079
Little pull? Huh?

408
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:20,122
You like that, right?

409
00:22:21,884 --> 00:22:24,004
You know what you are?

410
00:22:24,046 --> 00:22:26,166
You're a fucking
toll booth operator.

411
00:22:26,208 --> 00:22:28,288
You're gonna want
to leave right now.

412
00:22:28,330 --> 00:22:30,731
All right,
everything's fine.

413
00:22:30,773 --> 00:22:32,333
Everything's okay.

414
00:22:32,375 --> 00:22:34,417
We're gonna go right now.
Let's go.

415
00:22:50,913 --> 00:22:52,915
You okay?

416
00:22:53,596 --> 00:22:55,916
Why were they
talking about Nathan?

417
00:22:55,958 --> 00:22:57,960
Why do they
think he's alive?

418
00:23:01,203 --> 00:23:02,483
What was that?

419
00:23:02,525 --> 00:23:04,405
What was what?

420
00:23:04,447 --> 00:23:05,566
You wanna figure
this thing out

421
00:23:05,608 --> 00:23:07,287
or you wanna be
everyone's friend?

422
00:23:07,329 --> 00:23:09,450
Look, I saw the look
on her face when you
asked her about Nathan.

423
00:23:09,492 --> 00:23:10,611
She doesn't know anything.

424
00:23:10,653 --> 00:23:11,932
Well, Donna might.

425
00:23:11,974 --> 00:23:14,375
No, that's exactly
what we cannot...

426
00:23:14,417 --> 00:23:16,497
We cannot go around
assuming every little thing.

427
00:23:16,539 --> 00:23:18,541
Okay, look.

428
00:23:19,101 --> 00:23:20,861
We need to watch.

429
00:23:20,903 --> 00:23:21,902
What?

430
00:23:21,944 --> 00:23:23,384
It's what you said
about people

431
00:23:23,426 --> 00:23:25,786
keeping their shades drawn
at night.

432
00:23:25,828 --> 00:23:27,548
These things that
come from the forest,

433
00:23:27,590 --> 00:23:28,749
we need to see what they do

434
00:23:28,791 --> 00:23:30,793
when they don't know
they're being watched.

435
00:23:31,714 --> 00:23:32,873
And how to do that?

436
00:23:32,915 --> 00:23:36,677
You go back to the bus,
go about your day.

437
00:23:36,719 --> 00:23:38,439
When it gets closer to dark,
you sneak out,

438
00:23:38,481 --> 00:23:40,841
you meet me at the RV.
We'll stay the night
out there.

439
00:23:40,883 --> 00:23:43,566
Maybe see some things
they don't want us to see.

440
00:23:50,052 --> 00:23:51,211
Hey.

441
00:23:51,253 --> 00:23:52,292
Dad!

442
00:23:52,334 --> 00:23:53,534
Hey, how's it going
in here?

443
00:23:53,576 --> 00:23:55,536
Good, we're just
getting ready to clean up.

444
00:23:55,578 --> 00:23:56,897
Where's your mom?

445
00:23:56,939 --> 00:23:59,339
She said she was
going to Colony House.

446
00:23:59,381 --> 00:24:02,302
Victor and Jade were in here,
and Jade started
yelling at him.

447
00:24:02,344 --> 00:24:04,346
So I think Mom just
went to go check on him.

448
00:24:09,151 --> 00:24:10,951
Are you okay?

449
00:24:10,993 --> 00:24:13,435
Yeah, come here. I wanna
talk to you for a second.

450
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:19,480
What's up?

451
00:24:19,522 --> 00:24:21,524
I'm not gonna be
home tonight.

452
00:24:21,964 --> 00:24:23,323
I've got an idea,

453
00:24:23,365 --> 00:24:25,285
something that can
get us outta here.

454
00:24:25,327 --> 00:24:27,167
I just need some
time to figure it out.

455
00:24:27,209 --> 00:24:28,929
But I'm gonna be fine.

456
00:24:28,971 --> 00:24:31,331
I got a talisman,
I'm gonna be inside.

457
00:24:31,373 --> 00:24:32,453
Inside where?

458
00:24:32,495 --> 00:24:34,535
I'm gonna stay
the night in the RV.

459
00:24:34,577 --> 00:24:36,899
I'm telling you this
so you won't worry.

460
00:24:38,300 --> 00:24:41,301
When you see your mom,
you tell her I'm all right.

461
00:24:41,343 --> 00:24:43,345
Okay?

462
00:24:43,666 --> 00:24:45,265
Please be careful.

463
00:24:45,307 --> 00:24:47,309
Always.

464
00:24:54,236 --> 00:24:56,677
Jim. Can I have a word?

465
00:24:56,719 --> 00:24:59,241
Look, if this is
about before...
You some kind of moron?

466
00:25:00,523 --> 00:25:02,362
What?

467
00:25:02,404 --> 00:25:04,406
What is wrong
with you?

468
00:25:06,769 --> 00:25:10,290
I'm just looking for answers,
same as everybody else.

469
00:25:10,332 --> 00:25:11,972
By taunting Sara?

470
00:25:12,014 --> 00:25:13,534
Come on.

471
00:25:13,576 --> 00:25:15,976
You asked if her
brother was still alive.

472
00:25:16,018 --> 00:25:18,380
Look, I tried to
talk to you about this.

473
00:25:19,822 --> 00:25:21,301
Oh, Jesus Christ.

474
00:25:21,343 --> 00:25:23,263
Is this about that
fucking voice on the radio?

475
00:25:23,305 --> 00:25:24,785
Why do you say it
like it's strange

476
00:25:24,827 --> 00:25:26,306
that I don't wanna
just let it go?

477
00:25:26,348 --> 00:25:30,190
Don't even tell me you put
this shit in Randall's head.

478
00:25:30,232 --> 00:25:31,271
Listen...

479
00:25:31,313 --> 00:25:33,193
No, you fucking listen.

480
00:25:33,235 --> 00:25:34,755
That guy is
a fucking powder keg.

481
00:25:34,797 --> 00:25:36,637
If you start putting
ideas in his head, we...

482
00:25:36,679 --> 00:25:40,122
I didn't tell him
about the voice, okay?

483
00:25:41,564 --> 00:25:44,084
Talking to Sara was stupid.

484
00:25:44,126 --> 00:25:45,766
I get it.

485
00:25:45,808 --> 00:25:47,810
We all just wanna
go home.

486
00:25:49,331 --> 00:25:51,333
Are we done?

487
00:25:52,094 --> 00:25:53,133
Yeah.

488
00:25:53,175 --> 00:25:55,177
Okay.

489
00:26:04,146 --> 00:26:06,226
Victor, I need you
to be brave.

490
00:26:07,750 --> 00:26:09,029
But I'm scared.

491
00:26:09,071 --> 00:26:10,510
Everything's gonna
be okay.

492
00:26:10,552 --> 00:26:12,554
You just...

493
00:26:13,155 --> 00:26:15,035
You just draw
your pictures.

494
00:26:15,077 --> 00:26:17,037
And no matter
what happens,

495
00:26:17,079 --> 00:26:19,279
you do not come
out until morning.

496
00:26:19,321 --> 00:26:21,483
I love you.

497
00:26:24,446 --> 00:26:26,448
Mom!

498
00:26:58,560 --> 00:27:00,562
Hello.
Hello.

499
00:27:02,244 --> 00:27:04,246
May I come in?

500
00:27:05,327 --> 00:27:07,329
Yeah.

501
00:27:11,333 --> 00:27:16,056
I just wanted to say thank you
for the coat you gave Ethan.

502
00:27:16,098 --> 00:27:17,577
That's very thoughtful
of you.

503
00:27:17,619 --> 00:27:19,621
Hm.

504
00:27:22,464 --> 00:27:24,466
I remember these.

505
00:27:25,387 --> 00:27:27,347
Ethan said he found it
in one of the pockets,

506
00:27:27,389 --> 00:27:29,391
that you were upset.

507
00:27:30,472 --> 00:27:32,312
Can I have that,
please?

508
00:27:32,354 --> 00:27:34,915
Yeah, of course.

509
00:27:34,957 --> 00:27:39,842
Yeah, I... I hadn't...
I hadn't seen it
in a long time.

510
00:27:43,245 --> 00:27:45,247
Victor...

511
00:27:47,810 --> 00:27:51,053
Why didn't you tell
Jade we saw
that symbol in the tunnels?

512
00:27:52,975 --> 00:27:55,776
Because, it's not
good to ask questions.

513
00:27:55,818 --> 00:27:57,820
It's not good.

514
00:28:00,182 --> 00:28:02,302
People shouldn't
go looking for answers.

515
00:28:02,344 --> 00:28:04,346
Why not?

516
00:28:06,548 --> 00:28:08,550
'Cause they don't come back.

517
00:28:11,033 --> 00:28:14,194
But looking for answers
is our only way out.

